2>Words you'll hear today</h2></div><div class=3D"prose"><ul><li>Agent Regi=
stry =E2=80=94 the official catalog of the agents you run. It answers "what=
 do we have?" Note that it is a record of what got registered, not a live s=
can of what is running.</li><li>Agent Identity =E2=80=94 a unique, tamper-p=
roof ID badge for a single agent, so every action can be traced to exactly =
one of them. It answers "who did it?"</li><li>Service account =E2=80=94 a l=
ogin used by software rather than a person. When several agents share one, =
every action they take looks identical in the logs.</li><li>MCP =E2=80=94 t=
he controlled doorway an agent uses to reach data, instead of reaching into=
 the database directly.</li></ul><p>In one line, the fix you are heading to=
wards: replace one shared service account with a per-agent Agent Identity, =
so every action ties to exactly one agent and each agent gets only the acce=
ss its job needs. But first you have to see the problem clearly, which is w=
hat M0 is for.</p><figure class=3D"fig"><img class=3D"figimg" alt=3D"Four e=
